<title>UK: Continental Air ups ex-UK cargo rates 5pct.</title>
<headline>Continental Air ups ex-UK cargo rates 5pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines will raise its ex-UK cargo rates by an average of five percent to all destinations it serves in the United States, UK cargo manager Brian Coleman told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We think this is a fair increase because rates are currently pretty low,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Continental flies from London Gatwick and Manchester to New York Newark and Houston with DC-10 passenger aircraft.</p>
<p>Cargo is trucked to onward points throughout the U.S. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
</text>
